1
00:00:03,849 --> 00:00:06,253
The Lives of the Prophets, Part 1

2
00:00:06,769 --> 00:00:10,452
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:10,682 --> 00:00:16,875
قَالُوٓا۟ أَجِئْتَنَا لِتَأْفِكَنَا عَنْ ءَالِهَتِنَا فَأْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ

4
00:00:17,089 --> 00:00:23,114
 فَأْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّـٰدِقِينَ۝

5
00:00:23,209 --> 00:00:26,713
They said: “Have you come to turn us away from our gods?

6
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:30,594
Then bring us that which you threaten us, if you are one of the truthful.

7
00:00:30,634 --> 00:00:31,589
Now they challenged him.

8
00:00:31,795 --> 00:00:34,875
They told him: Bring us the punishment if you are telling the truth.

9
00:00:36,462 --> 00:00:42,459
And they were arrogant and proud because of their strength and their power and their so-called civilization.

10
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:46,125
By the way, we’re using this word “civilization” just because it’s commonly used,

11
00:00:46,244 --> 00:00:50,273
but we’re not using it in the positive sense of the word

12
00:00:50,329 --> 00:00:55,981
because always this word is used, or most of the time it’s used, to refer to Jahiliyyah(جاهلية).

13
00:00:56,647 --> 00:01:01,593
It is used to refer to ignorance, nations that disbelieved in Allah

14
00:01:01,815 --> 00:01:08,503
and the only reason why they are looked up at is because of their materialistic achievements.

15
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:17,942
They thought that this civilization of theirs and this wealth of theirs and this strength will save them from the punishment of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

16
00:01:18,474 --> 00:01:26,427
And we see that trait - we see that trend, similar in all strong and powerful civilizations that disbelieve in Allah.

17
00:01:26,982 --> 00:01:32,795
 The great empire, Great Britain when they constructed a ship

18
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:36,449
that was the biggest and the most powerful in the world,

19
00:01:36,648 --> 00:01:41,243
they thought that they can conquer the sea and they named it the “Titanic”.

20
00:01:41,402 --> 00:01:43,880
Look at the name they chose; the “Titanic”.

21
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:49,737
And they thought that they can challenge Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ and the strength of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

22
00:01:50,554 --> 00:01:53,828
But whenever you try to challenge Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎, what will happen?

23
00:01:53,868 --> 00:01:58,892
This Titanic, this ship, that is supposed to conquer the sea

24
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:04,027
and it’s supposed to be the most powerful and greatest achievement of mankind,

25
00:02:04,201 --> 00:02:07,223
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ sank it on its first trip.

26
00:02:08,731 --> 00:02:14,335
And then the next civilization and powerful nation of the world, the United States;

27
00:02:15,025 --> 00:02:21,588
When they were building their spacecraft that will challenge the creation of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎,

28
00:02:21,731 --> 00:02:23,501
they called it the “Challenger”

29
00:02:24,025 --> 00:02:27,051
to challenge the strength of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎,

30
00:02:27,098 --> 00:02:31,318
and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ blew it up, but nobody learns the lessons.

31
00:02:32,993 --> 00:02:37,226
And the people of ʿAd(عاد) thought that their power and strength can avail them.

32
00:02:37,884 --> 00:02:39,400
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

33
00:02:39,781 --> 00:02:47,347
فَأَمَّا عَادٌ فَٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ ٱلْحَقِّ وَقَالُوا۟ مَنْ أَشَدُّ مِنَّا قُوَّةً ۖ

34
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:56,826
أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَهُمْ هُوَ أَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً ۖ وَكَانُوا۟ بِـَٔايَـٰتِنَا يَجْحَدُونَ۝

35
00:02:57,072 --> 00:02:58,115
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

36
00:02:58,147 --> 00:03:04,351
As for ʿAd(عاد), they were arrogant in the land without right, and they said;

37
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:07,050
Who is mightier than us in strength?

38
00:03:07,605 --> 00:03:08,915
Who is stronger than us?

39
00:03:09,074 --> 00:03:11,257
Who are you threatening us with Hud(هود)?

40
00:03:11,567 --> 00:03:13,590
Who are you threatening us with?

41
00:03:13,837 --> 00:03:16,156
You say that Allah can do anything against us?

42
00:03:16,291 --> 00:03:17,458
Do whatever you want.

43
00:03:17,696 --> 00:03:19,402
مَنْ أَشَدُّ مِنَّا قُوَّةً

44
00:03:19,481 --> 00:03:21,608
Who is more powerful than us?

45
00:03:21,886 --> 00:03:23,335
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

46
00:03:23,529 --> 00:03:27,716
أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَهُمْ هُوَ أَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً

47
00:03:28,351 --> 00:03:34,441
See they not that Allah, Who created them, was Mightier in strength than them?

48
00:03:35,274 --> 00:03:36,853
And they used to deny Our Ayaat(آيات).

49
00:03:36,933 --> 00:03:43,015
Don’t they realize, don’t they understand that Allah, the One, Who created them, is mightier than them?

50
00:03:43,245 --> 00:03:47,570
Allah’s the One who created them; Whatever strength they had is created by Allah.

51
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:52,189
So Hud (هود), at that point, made Duʿa(دعاء),

52
00:03:53,030 --> 00:03:56,974
and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said, Hud(هود) is saying;

53
00:03:57,403 --> 00:04:02,933
قَالَ رَبِّ ٱنصُرْنِى بِمَا كَذَّبُونِ۝

54
00:04:03,195 --> 00:04:06,242
He said: O my Lord, help me because they denied me.

55
00:04:07,417 --> 00:04:10,552
And the Duʿa(دعاء) of Hud(هود) reached to Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ - Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said;

56
00:04:10,615 --> 00:04:13,393
قَالَ عَمَّا قَلِيلٍ لَّيُصْبِحُنَّ نَـٰدِمِينَ۝

57
00:04:14,195 --> 00:04:19,010
And Allah said: In a little while, they are sure to be regretful.

58
00:04:19,574 --> 00:04:22,129
In a little while, they will be regretful.

59
00:04:24,341 --> 00:04:29,675
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ was taking the people of ʿAd(عاد) through a test to remind them.

60
00:04:30,230 --> 00:04:33,289
See, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is giving them chances.

61
00:04:34,138 --> 00:04:36,384
So, Allah did not bring the punishment at once.

62
00:04:36,543 --> 00:04:44,492
Allah has made them go through a period of drought to remind them with their weakness as human beings

63
00:04:44,921 --> 00:04:48,310
so that they may turn to Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ in Tawbah(توبة) and repentance.

64
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:51,679
So they went through a period of drought, they were receiving no rain,

65
00:04:52,008 --> 00:04:55,794
their crops were drying, they were going through this difficult time.

66
00:04:57,159 --> 00:05:02,804
But that wasn’t sufficient to turn their attention to the truth and to ask Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ for forgiveness.

67
00:05:03,883 --> 00:05:08,255
So now Hud(هود) made the Duʿa(دعاء), and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ accepted the Duʿa(دعاء).

68
00:05:09,056 --> 00:05:15,425
Clouds started approaching in the horizon dark clouds

69
00:05:15,822 --> 00:05:22,267
and there’s a story that is mentioned that they went to Al-Kaʿbah(ٱلكعبة) to ask Allah for rain,

70
00:05:22,481 --> 00:05:24,840
and then they heard a voice that told them;

71
00:05:24,956 --> 00:05:28,218
Choose whichever cloud you want: the red or the white or the black.

72
00:05:28,258 --> 00:05:29,726
They said: We want the black cloud.

73
00:05:29,806 --> 00:05:36,448
Anyway, so these clouds were approaching their nation,

74
00:05:36,504 --> 00:05:38,575
and they saw these clouds in the horizon.

75
00:05:40,163 --> 00:05:41,172
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

76
00:05:41,212 --> 00:05:48,823
فَلَمَّا رَأَوْهُ عَارِضًا مُّسْتَقْبِلَ أَوْدِيَتِهِمْ قَالُوا۟ هَـٰذَا عَارِضٌ مُّمْطِرُنَا۝

77
00:05:48,863 --> 00:05:53,836
Then when they saw it as dense cloud coming towards their valleys, they said;

78
00:05:53,987 --> 00:05:55,955
This is a cloud bringing us rain.

79
00:05:56,257 --> 00:05:58,562
Because this was very dark, and a dark cloud means what?

80
00:05:59,070 --> 00:05:59,930
A lot of rain.

81
00:06:00,165 --> 00:06:05,222
So, they were looking forward and happy and pleased that we are finally receiving rain.

82
00:06:05,484 --> 00:06:06,730
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

83
00:06:06,770 --> 00:06:13,421
بَلْ هُوَ مَا ٱسْتَعْجَلْتُم بِهِۦ ۖ رِيحٌ فِيهَا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ۝

84
00:06:13,485 --> 00:06:17,096
Nay, but it is a torment which you were asking for,

85
00:06:17,207 --> 00:06:22,141
this is the torment you were asking for, a wind wherein is a painful torment.

86
00:06:22,315 --> 00:06:24,919
تُدَمِّرُ كُلَّ شَىْءٍۭ بِأَمْرِ رَبِّهَا۝

87
00:06:25,165 --> 00:06:28,463
destroying everything by the command of its Lord.

88
00:06:29,763 --> 00:06:33,335
They thought it was rain, it was the punishment of Allah.

89
00:06:34,136 --> 00:06:38,970
Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he would see clouds approaching Madina(مدينة), his face would change.

90
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:44,387
You can see that he’s worried, and ʿAishah(عائشة) would notice that,

91
00:06:44,745 --> 00:06:46,753
and she asked Rasool Allah ﷺ - she said;

92
00:06:46,793 --> 00:06:49,421
O Rasul Ullah, when people see the clouds, they’re happy,

93
00:06:49,651 --> 00:06:52,254
especially in Arabia because they don’t receive a lot of rain

94
00:06:52,437 --> 00:06:55,108
when people see the clouds coming, they’re happy, they’re very pleased.

95
00:06:55,783 --> 00:06:56,440
So ʿAishah(عائشة) said;

96
00:06:56,480 --> 00:07:01,697
When people see the clouds approaching, they’re happy, but you look anxious.

97
00:07:02,538 --> 00:07:09,079
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Because a nation before us saw these clouds, and thought that they had mercy.

98
00:07:09,309 --> 00:07:12,952
They didn’t know that it had the punishment of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ in them.

99
00:07:14,222 --> 00:07:16,666
Rasool Allah ﷺ had the fear in his heart,

100
00:07:17,991 --> 00:07:25,434
and we, unfortunately, in the world today in general, are exactly like the people of ʿAd(عاد).

101
00:07:27,236 --> 00:07:37,330
Exactly! you know, when the earthquake that happened few weeks ago and we felt it here in San Diego?

102
00:07:38,156 --> 00:07:42,599
The next day, I watched some of the interviews they made with people.

103
00:07:43,114 --> 00:07:46,845
They brought this lady; this lady said it was cool.

104
00:07:47,233 --> 00:07:49,545
Another guy said it was fun.

105
00:07:50,065 --> 00:07:52,032
Somebody else said it was an adventure.

106
00:07:52,491 --> 00:07:54,202
Others said it was interesting.

107
00:07:54,581 --> 00:07:57,535
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Allah is sending you these as a reminder.

108
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:03,781
Allah’s sending you these Ayaat(آيات) as a reminder, and you’re saying that they’re cool and fun and interesting and an adventure?

109
00:08:04,288 --> 00:08:10,094
Look at the state of the hearts of people, exactly like the people of ʿAd(عاد),

110
00:08:10,641 --> 00:08:13,754
because they are keeping Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ out of the equation.

111
00:08:14,142 --> 00:08:20,721
And that is the situation of the people today; they only think in terms of natural phenomena and natural laws

112
00:08:20,941 --> 00:08:23,261
as if Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ does not exist.

113
00:08:24,284 --> 00:08:25,862
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

114
00:08:26,869 --> 00:08:33,941
فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيحًا صَرْصَرًا فِىٓ أَيَّامٍ نَّحِسَاتٍ لِّنُذِيقَهُمْ

115
00:08:34,179 --> 00:08:38,197
لِّنُذِيقَهُمْ عَذَابَ ٱلْخِزْىِ فِى ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا ۖ

116
00:08:38,321 --> 00:08:43,118
وَلَعَذَابُ ٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ أَخْزَىٰ ۖ وَهُمْ لَا يُنصَرُونَ۝

117
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:49,512
So We sent upon them furious wind in days of evil omen for them.

118
00:08:50,570 --> 00:08:52,369
رِيحًا صَرْصَرًا

119
00:08:52,775 --> 00:09:02,984
Sarsar(صرصر) is explained as cold, severely cold and very ringing and loud voice, and very furious.

120
00:09:03,424 --> 00:09:05,805
This is the wind Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ sent on them.

121
00:09:07,014 --> 00:09:10,417
The closest thing that we have today similar to that is what?

122
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,031
The tornado.

123
00:09:12,384 --> 00:09:20,515
Because the tornado, if you have seen it, it is very fast wind and it has a very loud voice.

124
00:09:20,630 --> 00:09:26,263
I mean, if you heard, if you saw it on TV, it has an unbelievably loud sound.

125
00:09:27,163 --> 00:09:28,865
And it could be very cold.

126
00:09:30,346 --> 00:09:31,528
فِىٓ أَيَّامٍ نَّحِسَاتٍ

127
00:09:31,568 --> 00:09:33,486
In evil omen days on them.

128
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:37,533
 Tornados, it starts as a funnel in the cloud

129
00:09:38,724 --> 00:09:43,116
and then it makes a touchdown and it starts moving,

130
00:09:43,777 --> 00:09:46,756
and it would stay in one place only for a few minutes

131
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,415
and then it would keep on moving.

132
00:09:48,698 --> 00:09:53,513
It doesn’t stay for long in the same place just a few minutes and it keeps on moving.

133
00:09:54,341 --> 00:09:57,331
But, it’s leaving behind it a trail of destruction.

134
00:09:57,834 --> 00:10:03,636
In those few moments in those few minutes, it destroys everything that it passes over.

135
00:10:03,804 --> 00:10:06,511
It just rolls over everything and it destroys it.

136
00:10:07,181 --> 00:10:15,371
And we’ve seen that, in a few minutes, a tornado can make a touchdown and travel for a few miles and destroy everything.

137
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:20,241
This wind that Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ sent on the people of ʿAd(عاد)

138
00:10:20,470 --> 00:10:27,013
Allah besieged them, so imagine a tornado coming down and besieging the whole nation, surrounding it from every side.

139
00:10:27,675 --> 00:10:34,787
And it did not stay there for a few minutes, but it stayed there slamming them for 7 nights and 8 days.

140
00:10:34,963 --> 00:10:38,422
Imagine a tornado besieging the whole nation of ʿAd(عاد),

141
00:10:38,505 --> 00:10:44,117
surrounding them from every side, and this wind is violently turning with high speed,

142
00:10:44,390 --> 00:10:49,496
slamming their bodies against walls and against trees and against their homes, and destroying everything.

143
00:10:49,734 --> 00:10:56,385
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ put them under that siege for 8 days and 7 nights, and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

144
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,806
 حُسُومًا

145
00:10:57,867 --> 00:11:03,810
Husuma(حسوما) means continuously without giving them a break, giving them no break, no chance to even breathe.

146
00:11:04,465 --> 00:11:05,762
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

147
00:11:05,912 --> 00:11:12,645
سَخَّرَهَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَبْعَ لَيَالٍ وَثَمَـٰنِيَةَ أَيَّامٍ حُسُومًا۝

148
00:11:12,742 --> 00:11:16,673
And as for ʿAd(عاد), they were destroyed with a furious violent wind

149
00:11:16,938 --> 00:11:25,497
which Allah imposed on them for 7 nights and 8 days in succession, with persistence and giving them no break.

150
00:11:26,696 --> 00:11:28,698
That’s the punishment of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

151
00:11:28,830 --> 00:11:34,204
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is Shadid ul-ʿIqab(شديد العقاب), His punishment is severe, it is serious.

152
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:36,391
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

153
00:11:36,603 --> 00:11:43,089
لِّنُذِيقَهُمْ عَذَابَ ٱلْخِزْىِ فِى ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا ۖ وَلَعَذَابُ ٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ أَخْزَىٰ ۖ وَهُمْ لَا يُنصَرُونَ۝

154
00:11:43,547 --> 00:11:51,316
Allah says: That We might give them a taste of disgracing torment in this present world,

155
00:11:51,678 --> 00:11:57,251
but surely the torment of the Hereafter will be more disgracing, and they will never be helped.

156
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:03,358
This is the punishment of this world, but the punishment of the Akhirah(آخرة) is even more severe.

157
00:12:04,875 --> 00:12:06,400
What was the result?

158
00:12:07,168 --> 00:12:14,699
When the dust settled down and you walk into the nation of ʿAd(عاد), what do you see?

159
00:12:15,656 --> 00:12:17,097
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

160
00:12:17,137 --> 00:12:24,670
فَتَرَى ٱلْقَوْمَ فِيهَا صَرْعَىٰ كَأَنَّهُمْ أَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ خَاوِيَةٍ۝

161
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:33,143
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says: So that you could see men lying over throne as if they were hollow trunks of palm trees.

162
00:12:34,263 --> 00:12:35,643
These were very tall men,

163
00:12:36,057 --> 00:12:42,406
so Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said they are like palm trees that are knocked down, upside down, lying dead.

164
00:12:42,768 --> 00:12:45,583
And then Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ asks us this question,

165
00:12:46,782 --> 00:12:48,811
and this would go back to what I said before.

166
00:12:49,066 --> 00:12:54,181
If Allah did not tell us about the people of ʿAd(عاد) and where the people of ʿAd(عاد) lived, we wouldn’t have known.

167
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,077
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

168
00:12:56,147 --> 00:13:00,539
فَهَلْ تَرَىٰ لَهُم مِّنۢ بَاقِيَةٍ۝

169
00:13:00,610 --> 00:13:02,761
Do you see any remnants of the people of ʿAd(عاد)?

170
00:13:04,381 --> 00:13:09,793
We have remnants from the people of Firʿawn(فرعون), Al-Ahram Al-Awtad(الأهرام الأوتاد), the pyramids;

171
00:13:10,272 --> 00:13:14,660
we have remnants from Thamud(ثمود), Diyar Thamud(ديار ثمود), the dwellings of Thamud(ثمود);

172
00:13:15,119 --> 00:13:17,015
we have remnants from the Greek Empire;

173
00:13:17,262 --> 00:13:19,078
we have remnants from the Roman Empire;

174
00:13:19,290 --> 00:13:22,250
but from the empire of ʿAd(عاد), we have nothing.

175
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:27,964
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ completely destroyed them because they were the most powerful.

176
00:13:29,381 --> 00:13:32,485
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ completely erased them from the face of the earth,

177
00:13:33,124 --> 00:13:35,896
and now it is a land called Al-Ahqaf (الأحقاف), sand dunes.

178
00:13:35,936 --> 00:13:37,907
You don’t even see nothing, nobody even lives there.

179
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:41,937
It’s a desert now in Hadramaut(حضرموت), known Al-Ahqaf(الأحقاف), it’s a desert, empty.

180
00:13:44,151 --> 00:13:46,912
This is the nation which Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ said;

181
00:13:47,018 --> 00:13:49,787
إِرَمَ ذَاتِ ٱلْعِمَادِ ۝ ٱلَّتِى لَمْ يُخْلَقْ مِثْلُهَا فِى ٱلْبِلَـٰدِ۝

182
00:13:50,809 --> 00:13:55,312
Iram(إرم), the land of pillars which no other land was similar to.

183
00:13:56,203 --> 00:13:58,698
Nothing remained, they were destroyed completely.

184
00:13:59,845 --> 00:14:03,095
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ saved Hud(هود);

185
00:14:03,615 --> 00:14:23,971
وَلَمَّا جَآءَ أَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا هُودًا وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ مَعَهُۥ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَنَجَّيْنَـٰهُم مِّنْ عَذَابٍ غَلِيظٍ ۝

186
00:14:24,667 --> 00:14:35,525
وَتِلْكَ عَادٌ ۖ جَحَدُوا۟ بِـَٔايَـٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَعَصَوْا۟ رُسُلَهُۥ وَٱتَّبَعُوٓا۟

187
00:14:36,098 --> 00:14:43,400
 وَٱتَّبَعُوٓا۟ أَمْرَ كُلِّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيدٍ ۝

188
00:14:43,903 --> 00:14:52,342
وَأُتْبِعُوا۟ فِى هَـٰذِهِ ٱلدُّنْيَا لَعْنَةً وَيَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَـٰمَةِ ۗ

189
00:14:52,651 --> 00:14:59,450
أَلَآ إِنَّ عَادًا كَفَرُوا۟ رَبَّهُمْ ۗ

190
00:14:59,953 --> 00:15:05,341
أَلَا بُعْدًا لِّعَادٍ قَوْمِ هُودٍ۝

191
00:15:05,588 --> 00:15:13,072
Allah says: And when Our Commandment came, We saved Hud(هود) and those who believed with him by a Mercy from Us,

192
00:15:13,354 --> 00:15:15,665
and We saved them from a severe torment.

193
00:15:15,797 --> 00:15:20,535
Such were ʿAd(عاد); they rejected the Signs of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎

194
00:15:20,650 --> 00:15:25,694
and disobeyed His Messengers and followed the command of every proud obstinate.

195
00:15:26,549 --> 00:15:32,681
And they were pursued by a curse in this world, and on the Day of Resurrection,

196
00:15:32,866 --> 00:15:39,191
no doubt; verily, ʿAd(عاد) disbelieved in their Lord, so away with ʿAd(عاد), the people of Hud(هود).

197
00:15:41,854 --> 00:15:43,106
Their wealth didn’t help them.

198
00:15:45,117 --> 00:15:46,910
Their power didn’t do them any good.

199
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:52,421
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ completely destroyed them, destroyed them completely,

200
00:15:52,968 --> 00:15:57,788
and whoever follows the tracts of ʿAd(عاد), the same thing will happen to them.

201
00:15:57,991 --> 00:16:02,753
And I would like to close with this saying of Sayyidina Abu ad-Darda(سيدنا أبو الدرداء).

202
00:16:03,899 --> 00:16:10,852
Sayyidina Abu ad-Darda(سيدنا أبو الدرداء) was in Damascus, the capital of the Islamic Khilafah(خلافة) at the time,

203
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:16,463
 and he saw the extravagance of the Muslim Ummah(أمة).

204
00:16:17,371 --> 00:16:19,797
The Muslims were so wealthy at that time

205
00:16:20,405 --> 00:16:26,474
and the lifestyle of the Muslims was changing, now they had so much wealth, so their lifestyle was changing.

206
00:16:27,407 --> 00:16:33,316
Abu ad-Darda(أبو الدرداء) was on the strict ways that he was living on in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ;

207
00:16:33,356 --> 00:16:35,672
he did not change and he did not want the people to change.

208
00:16:36,573 --> 00:16:40,682
So, he stood up in Damascus and he said;

209
00:16:41,194 --> 00:16:46,100
يا أهل دمشق ! يا أهل دمشق، ألا تستحيون ؟

210
00:16:47,105 --> 00:16:51,814
 تجمعون ما لا تأكلون وتبنون ما لا تسكنون،

211
00:16:52,193 --> 00:16:59,583
 وتأملون ما لا تطيلون، وإن من كان قبلكم كانوا يجمعون فيوعون،

212
00:16:59,905 --> 00:17:04,302
ويبنون فيوثقون، ويعملون فيطيلون،

213
00:17:04,734 --> 00:17:11,163
فأصبح جمعهم بورا، ومساكنهم قبورا، وأملهم غرورا،

214
00:17:11,286 --> 00:17:20,121
الا ان عاد ملكت ما بين عدن وعمان، خيل وركبانا فمن يشتري مني نير ثعاد بدرهمين ؟

215
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:28,080
Abu ad-Darda(أبو الدرداء) said: “O people of Damascus! O people of Damascus, don’t you have any shame?

216
00:17:29,208 --> 00:17:31,869
You are gathering wealth that you will not use,

217
00:17:32,734 --> 00:17:36,808
and you are building palaces which you will not live in,

218
00:17:37,478 --> 00:17:40,855
and you are expecting to live longer than your life,

219
00:17:41,948 --> 00:17:46,507
and the people before you, they used to gather and use what they gathered,

220
00:17:46,675 --> 00:17:49,778
and they used to build and they would build better than you,

221
00:17:49,964 --> 00:17:52,361
and they used to live longer than your life,

222
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:59,248
but then, whatever they gathered did not do them any good, and their palaces became their graveyards,

223
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:01,389
and their desires were false.

224
00:18:01,883 --> 00:18:08,523
And remember that the people of ʿAd(عاد) had an army that extends from ʿAdan(عدن) up to ʿOman(عمان);

225
00:18:09,485 --> 00:18:13,373
who will buy from me the remnants of ʿAd(عاد) with 2 dirhams(درهم)?

226
00:18:13,796 --> 00:18:17,797
Who’s gonna buy from me the inheritance of ʿAd(عاد) with 2 dirhams(درهم)?

227
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:18,805
They left nothing.

228
00:18:19,237 --> 00:18:25,740
This huge nation, if you would put it in the auction to sell it, it will not even fetch a dollar for you.

229
00:18:26,084 --> 00:18:27,248
There’s nothing left.

230
00:18:28,994 --> 00:18:32,540
So, we need to remember that whatever we see around us will not do us any good,

231
00:18:32,795 --> 00:18:38,607
and if we disbelieve in Allah and the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah, and disbelieve in the Messenger of Allah like ʿAd(عاد) did,

232
00:18:39,109 --> 00:18:43,003
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ will include us in severe punishment.

233
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:47,044
And if we stick to the truth that we have that we have with us now,

234
00:18:47,362 --> 00:18:50,485
and we keep away from the ways of the nonbelievers,

235
00:18:50,776 --> 00:18:56,206
and have our unique identity, and we are proud with what Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has given us,

236
00:18:56,523 --> 00:18:59,645
then whenever Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ punishes the nonbelievers,

237
00:18:59,812 --> 00:19:02,581
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ would save the ones who believed in Him.

238
00:19:03,005 --> 00:19:05,070
We’ll start with the story of Sayyidina Salih(سيدنا صالح).

239
00:19:05,218 --> 00:19:09,828
وَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ أَصْحَـٰبُ ٱلْحِجْرِ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

240
00:19:09,978 --> 00:19:13,099
And verily, the dwellers of the Hijr(ألحجر) denied the Messengers.

241
00:19:13,139 --> 00:19:15,601
Al-Hijr (ٱلحجر) is the rocky track.

242
00:19:16,130 --> 00:19:20,381
They used to live in a rocky track, it’s a very rocky area, solid rock.

243
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:26,911
وَءَاتَيْنَـٰهُمْ ءَايَـٰتِنَا فَكَانُوا۟ عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِينَ۝

244
00:19:27,017 --> 00:19:30,439
And We gave them Our Signs, but they were averse to Them.

245
00:19:30,536 --> 00:19:36,414
وَكَانُوا۟ يَنْحِتُونَ مِنَ ٱلْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًا ءَامِنِينَ۝

246
00:19:36,476 --> 00:19:41,987
They used to carve out of mountains houses, feeling secure.

247
00:19:42,217 --> 00:19:43,502
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

248
00:19:43,679 --> 00:19:51,113
They used to carve out these houses in the mountains, palaces in the mountains, Amineen(ءَامِنِينَ).

249
00:19:52,136 --> 00:19:55,929
In the tafsir (تفسير) of Ibn al-Jawzi (ابن الجوزي), he gives a few meanings of Amineen(ءَامِنِينَ).

250
00:19:56,652 --> 00:20:00,673
One of them is that they were feeling secure and safe from the punishment of Allah.

251
00:20:01,119 --> 00:20:06,861
The second meaning is that they were feeling secure and safe that these buildings will never be destroyed.

252
00:20:06,976 --> 00:20:09,286
 They’re carving it out of solid bedrock.

253
00:20:09,436 --> 00:20:15,795
Imagine you have a solid rock, like this Masjid(مسجد), and you carve into it a house.

254
00:20:15,861 --> 00:20:23,478
They were not building houses from bricks of stone; no, they were carving out houses in solid rock.

255
00:20:24,386 --> 00:20:25,554
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

256
00:20:25,594 --> 00:20:27,875
أَتُتْرَكُونَ فِى مَا هَـٰهُنَآ ءَامِنِينَ۝

257
00:20:28,095 --> 00:20:30,794
Will you be left secure in that which you have here?

258
00:20:31,076 --> 00:20:34,252
When you have a house carved in rock, what will destroy it?

259
00:20:34,622 --> 00:20:43,533
I mean, rock, solid rock, earthquake cannot harm it, wind cannot affect it - a hurricane, tornados…

260
00:20:43,727 --> 00:20:47,453
I mean, it’s rock, solid rock, you’re in the middle of a mountain.

261
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:50,529
So they used to feel that they’re secure from everything, nothing can harm them.

262
00:20:50,697 --> 00:20:56,800
Plus, they’re in high ground, so if there’s any floods, it will not affect them.

263
00:20:57,427 --> 00:21:05,015
They have a guaranteed safety - 100% sure, as they thought, Amineen(ءَامِنِينَ).

264
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:08,789
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎’s asking them: Do you think that you will be here, safe?

265
00:21:09,292 --> 00:21:13,993
A human being should never feel safe as long as he’s on the face of this earth.

266
00:21:15,334 --> 00:21:19,734
We should always be worried of the punishment of Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

267
00:21:21,066 --> 00:21:22,644
Therefore, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

268
00:21:22,684 --> 00:21:41,368
أَفَأَمِنُوا۟ مَكْرَ ٱللَّهِ ۚ فَلَا يَأْمَنُ مَكْرَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلْقَوْمُ ٱلْخَـٰسِرُونَ۝

269
00:21:41,554 --> 00:21:42,506
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

270
00:21:42,546 --> 00:21:47,227
The only ones who feel secure from the Planning of Allah are the losers.

271
00:21:47,633 --> 00:21:50,184
If you feel that you’re safe, you are a loser.

272
00:21:50,510 --> 00:21:52,592
The Mu’min(مؤمن) is always afraid.

273
00:21:52,918 --> 00:21:55,881
The Mu’min(مؤمن) always has fear from Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

274
00:21:56,507 --> 00:21:58,165
So their Nabi (نبي‎), Salih (صالح), is telling them;

275
00:21:58,205 --> 00:22:03,924
أَتُتْرَكُونَ فِى مَا هَـٰهُنَآ ءَامِنِينَ ۝

276
00:22:04,153 --> 00:22:08,727
 فِى جَنَّـٰتٍ وَعُيُونٍ ۝

277
00:22:08,991 --> 00:22:14,115
وَزُرُوعٍ وَنَخْلٍ طَلْعُهَا هَضِيمٌ ۝

278
00:22:14,389 --> 00:22:20,350
وَتَنْحِتُونَ مِنَ ٱلْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًا فَـٰرِهِينَ۝

279
00:22:20,390 --> 00:22:22,810
Will you be left secure in that which you have here?

280
00:22:22,934 --> 00:22:27,449
In gardens and springs, and cornfields and date palms with soft spadix?

281
00:22:27,669 --> 00:22:30,933
And you carve houses out of mountains with great skill.

282
00:22:32,141 --> 00:22:34,972
They had great skill, they were very excellent architects.

283
00:22:35,083 --> 00:22:39,401
They were great in construction and structures of their houses.

284
00:22:40,211 --> 00:22:41,385
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

285
00:22:41,482 --> 00:23:08,139
وَٱذْكُرُوٓا۟ إِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَآءَ مِنۢ بَعْدِ عَادٍ وَبَوَّأَكُمْ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ تَتَّخِذُونَ مِن سُهُولِهَا قُصُورًا

286
00:23:09,374 --> 00:23:34,186
 تَتَّخِذُونَ مِن سُهُولِهَا قُصُورًا وَتَنْحِتُونَ ٱلْجِبَالَ بُيُوتًا ۖ فَٱذْكُرُوٓا۟ ءَالَآءَ ٱللَّهِ

287
00:23:35,026 --> 00:23:50,652
فَٱذْكُرُوٓا۟ ءَالَآءَ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ۝

288
00:23:50,970 --> 00:23:52,747
What the people of Thamud(ثمود) used to do is

289
00:23:52,787 --> 00:23:58,294
they would build, they would carve out these houses in the mountain,

290
00:24:00,366 --> 00:24:04,466
and then they would build palaces on the valleys.

291
00:24:05,101 --> 00:24:09,862
So they have palaces in the valley, and they have these houses carved in the mountains.

292
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:16,154
But they were corrupt, and their Nabi(نبي‎), Salih(صالح), told them;

293
00:24:16,194 --> 00:24:18,218
وَلَا تَعْثَوْا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ۝

294
00:24:18,258 --> 00:24:21,287
Do not go about making mischief on the earth.

295
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:22,848
They were very corrupt people.

296
00:24:23,421 --> 00:24:25,234
What was the message of Sayyidina Salih(سيدنا صالح)?

297
00:24:25,411 --> 00:24:30,331
وَإِلَىٰ ثَمُودَ أَخَاهُمْ صَـٰلِحًا ۚ

298
00:24:30,463 --> 00:24:38,822
قَالَ يَـٰقَوْمِ ٱعْبُدُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ

299
00:24:39,201 --> 00:24:42,111
O my people, worship no god other than Allah.

300
00:24:42,358 --> 00:24:45,516
The same message of ʿAd(عاد) and the same message of Nuh(نوح).

301
00:24:45,684 --> 00:24:48,109
And he repeated the same thing that they did.

302
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:49,828
What did they also say?

303
00:24:50,684 --> 00:24:51,896
ثُمَّ ٱسْتَغْفِرُوا۟ رَبَّكُمْ

304
00:24:52,011 --> 00:24:52,820
Istighfar(ٱستغفار).

305
00:24:53,175 --> 00:24:55,600
Every Nabi(نبي‎) is telling his people to make Istighfar(ٱستغفار).

306
00:24:56,517 --> 00:24:59,108
So, this was the Daʿwah (دعوة) of Sayyidina Salih(سيدنا صالح).

307
00:24:59,284 --> 00:25:00,854
What was the response?

308
00:25:01,322 --> 00:25:09,869
Sayyidina Salih(سيدنا صالح) was a young man, and he was very intelligent and strong, and he was from a noble family.

309
00:25:10,936 --> 00:25:13,281
He was from the high class of the society

310
00:25:14,569 --> 00:25:18,397
and they were preparing him to be their leader.

311
00:25:18,437 --> 00:25:24,845
He was a young man and they were looking forward that, one day, he will assume responsibility for the people of Thamud(ثمود).

312
00:25:25,392 --> 00:25:27,575
They had a lot of expectations in Salih(صالح),

313
00:25:28,519 --> 00:25:31,332
and suddenly Salih(صالح) presented them with the Message of Islam.

314
00:25:31,729 --> 00:25:32,684
So what happened?

315
00:25:32,949 --> 00:25:53,062
قَالُوا۟ يَـٰصَـٰلِحُ قَدْ كُنتَ فِينَا مَرْجُوًّا قَبْلَ هَـٰذَآ ۖ أَتَنْهَىٰنَآ أَن نَّعْبُدَ مَا يَعْبُدُ ءَابَآؤُنَا وَإِنَّنَا لَفِى شَكٍّ مِّمَّا تَدْعُونَآ إِلَيْهِ مُرِيبٍ۝

316
00:25:53,133 --> 00:25:57,889
 They said: O Salih(صالح), you have been among us as a figure of good hope.

317
00:25:58,061 --> 00:26:01,330
We had good expectations of you, till this.

318
00:26:01,645 --> 00:26:05,784
Do you now forbid us the worship of what our fathers have worshipped?

319
00:26:06,984 --> 00:26:15,385
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the disease and the illness that people have is that they do not want to give up what their fathers used to worship.

320
00:26:16,346 --> 00:26:18,947
Taqlid(تقليد) - imitation;

321
00:26:20,067 --> 00:26:27,873
we are willing to change, look at the people around you, take any nation on the face of the earth, advanced nation, Japan or the United States.

322
00:26:28,458 --> 00:26:32,943
Look at the difference between the United States now and the United States 100 or 200 years ago,

323
00:26:32,988 --> 00:26:36,276
or Japan of today and Japan of 200 years ago.

324
00:26:36,795 --> 00:26:41,274
Big difference, look at the advancement in technology and science,

325
00:26:41,512 --> 00:26:48,211
look at the different lifestyle, look at the standard of living, look at the way people think and speak and behave

326
00:26:48,432 --> 00:26:55,755
professors in math, professors in physics, experts in economics, experts in engineering, experts in medicine.

327
00:26:56,313 --> 00:27:03,685
 They learned a lot, there’s a big difference between one of them today and their forefathers 100 years ago.

328
00:27:04,602 --> 00:27:08,024
Big difference…in everything but religion.

329
00:27:10,070 --> 00:27:13,227
There’s a big difference in everything, but religion did not change.

330
00:27:14,179 --> 00:27:20,664
So this PhD in math who’s working in the most advanced lab in the world

331
00:27:20,894 --> 00:27:25,507
from 8 o’clock until 5 is dealing with logic and numbers,

332
00:27:26,309 --> 00:27:32,710
and then when he goes back home in the evening, he doesn’t have a problem making Sujud(سجود) to an idol or worshipping a cow.

333
00:27:33,353 --> 00:27:35,611
When it comes to religion, Shaytan(شيطان) is telling people;

334
00:27:35,651 --> 00:27:39,201
Don’t change. Stay on the religion, the false religion that you’re doing.

335
00:27:39,376 --> 00:27:47,865
إِنَّا وَجَدْنَآ ءَابَآءَنَا عَلَىٰٓ أُمَّةٍ وَإِنَّا

336
00:27:48,384 --> 00:27:54,081
وَإِنَّا عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَـٰرِهِم مُّهْتَدُونَ۝

337
00:27:54,142 --> 00:27:59,927
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says: We found our fathers following a certain religion, we’re gonna follow them.

338
00:28:02,070 --> 00:28:03,601
This is the disease and illness,

339
00:28:03,786 --> 00:28:04,756
but Shaytan(شيطان) is telling them;

340
00:28:04,796 --> 00:28:09,430
 No problem, go and advance in everything else, that's’s ok. Do whatever you want, that’s not gonna do you anything in Akhirah(آخرة).

341
00:28:10,153 --> 00:28:15,637
But in terms of religion, stay on the religion of the cow and the religion of Buddha(بدها) and the religion of the cross.

342
00:28:18,688 --> 00:28:23,199
So the people of Salih(صالح), they knew Salih عليه السلام, they knew him, and they knew his qualities,

343
00:28:23,239 --> 00:28:29,739
and they were looking ahead at giving him the responsibilities of leading their people,

344
00:28:29,907 --> 00:28:32,464
but when he came with Islam, they said: “Now we change our mind.”

345
00:28:32,632 --> 00:28:35,057
وَإِنَّنَا لَفِى شَكٍّ مِّمَّا تَدْعُونَآ إِلَيْهِ مُرِيبٍ۝

346
00:28:35,097 --> 00:28:36,942
Now we are in doubts of you.

347
00:28:37,753 --> 00:28:41,677
First, we used to have trust in you. Now when you’re Muslim, we’re doubting you.

348
00:28:42,330 --> 00:28:43,950
And then they accused him of magic;

349
00:28:44,082 --> 00:28:52,186
قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّمَآ أَنتَ مِنَ ٱلْمُسَحَّرِينَ۝

350
00:28:52,226 --> 00:28:54,521
They said: “You are only of those bewitched.

351
00:28:54,618 --> 00:29:01,793
 مَآ أَنتَ إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا فَأْتِ بِـَٔايَةٍ

352
00:29:02,075 --> 00:29:07,869
 فَأْتِ بِـَٔايَةٍ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّـٰدِقِينَ۝

353
00:29:07,922 --> 00:29:11,866
You are but a human being like us, then bring us a sign if you are truthful.

354
00:29:13,030 --> 00:29:14,441
They said they wanted a sign.

355
00:29:15,904 --> 00:29:17,104
What sign do you want?

356
00:29:17,492 --> 00:29:18,469
They were given the option.

357
00:29:18,637 --> 00:29:22,864
Thamud(ثمود) - the people of Thamud(ثمود) were given an option that was not given to the other nations.

358
00:29:23,252 --> 00:29:25,721
They got to choose their miracle.

359
00:29:28,005 --> 00:29:29,372
Salih(صالح) told them: “What do you want?

360
00:29:30,474 --> 00:29:33,271
They said: Do you see this rock over here?

361
00:29:33,994 --> 00:29:37,689
We want you to produce out of it a living camel.

362
00:29:39,135 --> 00:29:41,925
This solid rock, produce for us a camel.

363
00:29:43,151 --> 00:29:45,505
Sayyidina Salih(سيدنا صالح) asked Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

364
00:29:46,449 --> 00:29:49,280
The miracle was performed, Muʿjizah(معجزة).

365
00:29:49,782 --> 00:29:51,855
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ gives life to the dead.

366
00:29:53,751 --> 00:30:02,390
I mean, for Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎, what's the difference between creating from a cell, or creating from dirt, or creating from a rock?

367
00:30:03,113 --> 00:30:06,852
They’re all dead things, it’s no difference for Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

368
00:30:07,073 --> 00:30:08,378
It looks different to us.

369
00:30:08,739 --> 00:30:11,014
But for Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎, it’s;

370
00:30:11,120 --> 00:30:11,870
 كُنْ فَيَكُونُ

371
00:30:11,949 --> 00:30:13,069
Be, and it becomes.

372
00:30:13,501 --> 00:30:19,615
Suddenly out of this rock, and the people of Thamud(ثمود) are watching, a huge she-camel came out,

373
00:30:20,735 --> 00:30:23,424
 huge, bigger than the regular camels.

374
00:30:24,015 --> 00:30:25,467
Sayyidina Salih(سيدنا صالح) told them;

375
00:30:25,643 --> 00:30:27,186
This is the agreement.

376
00:30:27,389 --> 00:30:32,392
This camel that you asked for, you can drink from your water one day

377
00:30:32,445 --> 00:30:36,413
but then the next day, you have to allow the water for the camel. You don’t touch it.

378
00:30:36,916 --> 00:30:42,206
You can take from the wells today, but tomorrow, the next day, it’s only for the camel.

379
00:30:42,246 --> 00:30:46,315
You don’t drink any water. If you wanna drink, you can drink from the milk of the camel, but no water.

380
00:30:46,721 --> 00:30:54,922
قَالَ هَـٰذِهِۦ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُومٍ

381
00:30:54,962 --> 00:30:55,549
He said;

382
00:30:55,743 --> 00:31:03,080
Here is a she-camel, it has a right to drink water and you have a right to drink water, each on a day known.

383
00:31:03,312 --> 00:31:07,257
This is the schedule and then he told them;

384
00:31:07,460 --> 00:31:19,988
وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوٓءٍ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ۝

385
00:31:20,129 --> 00:31:24,244
And don’t touch it with any harm, otherwise you would be punished.

386
00:31:24,774 --> 00:31:28,945
So this was a sacred camel, you cannot touch it, you cannot harm it.

387
00:31:30,655 --> 00:31:34,052
So the camel was drinking from the well one day and they would drink one day,

388
00:31:36,098 --> 00:31:45,568
but there were some conspiracies occurring, there was something brewing.

389
00:31:46,820 --> 00:31:54,914
There were a group of men out of the people of Thamud(ثمود) who were planning not only to harm the camel - but to kill it.

390
00:31:56,060 --> 00:31:57,101
They were ordered;

391
00:31:57,224 --> 00:31:58,926
Don’t touch it with any harm.

392
00:31:59,376 --> 00:32:01,753
These were planning to kill the camel.

393
00:32:03,587 --> 00:32:05,201
How many men are these?

394
00:32:06,673 --> 00:32:07,846
How many do you expect?

395
00:32:09,028 --> 00:32:09,746
How many?

396
00:32:10,150 --> 00:32:10,988
9.

397
00:32:11,910 --> 00:32:18,592
Out of the whole nation of Thamud(ثمود), the ones who conspired to kill the camel were 9.

398
00:32:19,342 --> 00:32:20,664
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

399
00:32:20,779 --> 00:32:28,253
وَكَانَ فِى ٱلْمَدِينَةِ تِسْعَةُ رَهْطٍ يُفْسِدُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَا يُصْلِحُونَ۝

400
00:32:28,368 --> 00:32:30,952
And there were in the city 9 men.

401
00:32:31,251 --> 00:32:31,909
So the Ayah(آية) is;

402
00:32:31,949 --> 00:32:38,291
And there were in the city 9 men who made mischief in the land and would not reform.

403
00:32:38,556 --> 00:32:40,725
These were 9 men who were corrupt.

404
00:32:41,298 --> 00:32:45,946
They are the ones who made the conspiracy and planned to kill the camel.

405
00:32:46,131 --> 00:32:49,039
It wasn’t all of the people of Thamud(ثمود), it was only 9.

406
00:32:49,770 --> 00:32:53,924
These men agreed, and these were from the leaders of Thamud(ثمود).

407
00:32:54,374 --> 00:32:57,925
They came together and agreed: We’re gonna kill the camel.

408
00:32:59,865 --> 00:33:07,120
So they made their move, and when they got next to the camel, they hesitated because the camel was huge.

409
00:33:08,719 --> 00:33:18,422
 But one of them, the most evil among them, he took his sword and he hit the camel in its front legs

410
00:33:18,616 --> 00:33:19,942
and that is called “ʿAqar(عقر)”.

411
00:33:20,189 --> 00:33:24,343
So the camel fell down, and then they attacked it with their swords and killed it.

412
00:33:24,942 --> 00:33:26,503
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

413
00:33:26,689 --> 00:33:32,464
كَذَّبَتْ ثَمُودُ بِطَغْوَىٰهَآ ۝ إِذِ ٱنۢبَعَثَ أَشْقَىٰهَا۝

414
00:33:32,504 --> 00:33:36,768
Thamud denied their prophet when the most wicked man among them went forth.

415
00:33:37,429 --> 00:33:42,194
 So out of these 9, only one dared to make the attack on the camel.

416
00:33:42,300 --> 00:33:43,535
إِذِ ٱنۢبَعَثَ أَشْقَىٰهَا

417
00:33:43,649 --> 00:33:47,168
The most evil one, the wicked among them, he’s the one who made his attack.

418
00:33:47,327 --> 00:33:48,581
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

419
00:33:48,819 --> 00:33:50,327
 فَعَقَرُوه

420
00:33:50,557 --> 00:33:51,683
But they killed her.

421
00:33:51,723 --> 00:33:54,566
And “ʿAqar(عقر)” is when you chop the front legs.

422
00:33:54,738 --> 00:33:57,868
So the camel fell down and then they cut her into pieces.

423
00:33:58,216 --> 00:34:26,231
فَعَقَرُوا۟ ٱلنَّاقَةَ وَعَتَوْا۟ عَنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ وَقَالُوا۟ يَـٰصَـٰلِحُ ٱئْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

424
00:34:26,293 --> 00:34:31,328
So they killed the she-camel and insolently defied the Commandment of their Lord, and said;

425
00:34:31,557 --> 00:34:36,028
O Salih(صالح), bring about the threat if you are indeed one of the Messengers of Allah.

426
00:34:36,725 --> 00:34:38,815
The camel is dead, bring your threat.

427
00:34:39,406 --> 00:34:41,583
We challenge you, we dare you to do anything.

428
00:34:42,262 --> 00:34:47,958
Here’s the camel, you said this is the camel, this camel is sacred, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is protecting it, look at it, it’s dead.

429
00:34:48,523 --> 00:34:50,742
So now, bring us the punishment that you promised.

430
00:34:51,818 --> 00:34:57,021
Not only did they do that, they went back and they made a conspiracy at nighttime

431
00:34:57,233 --> 00:35:03,741
that they will assassinate not only Salih(صالح) but they would exterminate his whole family.

432
00:35:05,010 --> 00:35:09,665
They made a plan that “the next step - after we kill the camel - we’re gonna kill Salih(صالح) and all of his family.”

433
00:35:09,908 --> 00:35:15,509
قَالُوا۟ تَقَاسَمُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ لَنُبَيِّتَنَّهُۥ وَأَهْلَهُۥ

434
00:35:15,783 --> 00:35:23,986
ثُمَّ لَنَقُولَنَّ لِوَلِيِّهِۦ مَا شَهِدْنَا مَهْلِكَ أَهْلِهِۦ وَإِنَّا لَصَـٰدِقُونَ۝

435
00:35:24,026 --> 00:35:31,632
They said: “Swear one to another, by Allah, that we shall make a secret night attack on him and his household,

436
00:35:31,905 --> 00:35:35,046
 and afterwards we will surely say to his near relatives;

437
00:35:35,248 --> 00:35:39,146
We witnessed not the destruction of his household and verily, we are telling the truth.

438
00:35:39,613 --> 00:35:41,676
So they’re planning to kill Salih(صالح) and his family,

439
00:35:42,099 --> 00:35:45,503
and then they’re planning to lie and say that “we didn’t kill him,”

440
00:35:46,226 --> 00:35:48,016
and they’re gonna say that “we’re telling the truth.”

441
00:35:48,607 --> 00:35:52,830
Salih(صالح) came out and told his people;

442
00:35:53,879 --> 00:35:56,110
تَمَتَّعُوا۟ فِى دَارِكُمْ ثَلَـٰثَةَ أَيَّامٍ

443
00:35:57,556 --> 00:35:59,727
You have 3 days to enjoy yourselves.

444
00:36:01,720 --> 00:36:03,651
ذَٰلِكَ وَعْدٌ غَيْرُ مَكْذُوبٍ

445
00:36:03,721 --> 00:36:05,935
This is a promise that will not be belied.

446
00:36:05,975 --> 00:36:09,735
You have 3 days - 3 days to enjoy yourselves and that’s it.

447
00:36:09,955 --> 00:36:11,357
You’re not gonna live anymore.

448
00:36:13,095 --> 00:36:15,714
The first day passed - nothing happened.

449
00:36:16,287 --> 00:36:18,560
The second day passed - nothing happened.

450
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:20,517
The third day passed - nothing happened.

451
00:36:20,557 --> 00:36:22,202
They started joking at nighttime and saying

452
00:36:22,242 --> 00:36:26,769
Look at this liar, he told us 3 days - here, the 3 days is over.

453
00:36:27,052 --> 00:36:29,980
They went to bed - Amineen(ءَامِنِينَ), secure.

454
00:36:30,994 --> 00:36:32,164
Early in the morning;

455
00:36:32,466 --> 00:36:36,625
فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ ٱلصَّيْحَةُ مُصْبِحِينَ۝

456
00:36:36,665 --> 00:36:43,705
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ sent on them the awful cry in the morning of the 4th day, the exact deadline.

457
00:36:44,494 --> 00:36:46,989
They went to bed safe - Amineen(ءَامِنِينَ).

458
00:36:47,333 --> 00:36:52,560
In houses carved from solid bedrock, nothing can destroy it.

459
00:36:53,414 --> 00:37:03,416
Wind cannot harm it, earthquake will not do it any harm; a hurricane, a tornado, torrential rain, a storm, floods  will not harm it.

460
00:37:03,496 --> 00:37:04,902
They thought they were safe.

461
00:37:05,122 --> 00:37:10,052
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ destroyed them with a sound wave, an awful cry.

462
00:37:10,751 --> 00:37:16,064
Very, very loud voice that was so loud

463
00:37:17,143 --> 00:37:18,342
 فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ ٱلرَّجْفَةُ

464
00:37:18,382 --> 00:37:20,221
it caused the earth to shake.

465
00:37:20,856 --> 00:37:28,472
The cry, this awful cry, was so violent and powerful, it made the earth under them shake.

466
00:37:29,742 --> 00:37:33,031
Only nowadays are we learning the power of sound waves,

467
00:37:33,772 --> 00:37:41,901
and now we hear that they’re trying to use and they’re thinking about ways to use sound waves as a weapon.

468
00:37:43,215 --> 00:37:46,170
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ destroyed these people with sound.

469
00:37:46,663 --> 00:37:51,745
It is said that it was so violent that it shook their insides so their hearts were falling.

470
00:37:52,812 --> 00:37:56,913
It was so violent, no matter how strong your house is, it’s like a microwave.

471
00:37:57,927 --> 00:38:03,193
These are waves that came in and could pass through anything, through rock, through walls.

472
00:38:03,334 --> 00:38:05,945
It is a sound wave, it can go through anything.

473
00:38:06,015 --> 00:38:09,678
It can travel through any medium that Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ created.

474
00:38:09,718 --> 00:38:11,511
There’s nothing that can stop it.

475
00:38:11,828 --> 00:38:17,657
So the sound reached and it was shaking their insides so their hearts fell down dead.

476
00:38:19,341 --> 00:38:20,764
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

477
00:38:20,958 --> 00:38:29,131
وَأَخَذَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا۟ ٱلصَّيْحَةُ فَأَصْبَحُوا۟ فِى دِيَـٰرِهِمْ جَـٰثِمِينَ ۝ كَأَن لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا۟ فِيهَآ ۗ

478
00:38:29,237 --> 00:38:36,766
أَلَآ إِنَّ ثَمُودَا۟ كَفَرُوا۟ رَبَّهُمْ ۗ أَلَا بُعْدًا لِّثَمُودَ۝

479
00:38:36,934 --> 00:38:38,217
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

480
00:38:38,403 --> 00:38:45,205
And the awful cry overtook the wrongdoers, so they laid dead prostrate in their homes as if they never lived.

481
00:38:46,373 --> 00:38:47,929
As if they never lived.

482
00:38:48,493 --> 00:38:53,458
After moments of cry, as if nobody was living in Thamud(ثمود),

483
00:38:53,555 --> 00:38:57,136
it was a haunted, deserted area.

484
00:38:58,175 --> 00:39:01,376
أَلَآ إِنَّ ثَمُودَا۟ كَفَرُوا۟ رَبَّهُمْ ۗ أَلَا بُعْدًا لِّثَمُودَ۝

485
00:39:01,941 --> 00:39:06,032
Thamud(ثمود) disbelieved in their Lord, so away with Thamud(ثمود).

486
00:39:06,451 --> 00:39:07,915
With Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎, it’s;

487
00:39:07,955 --> 00:39:08,911
 كُنْ فَيَكُونُ

488
00:39:09,537 --> 00:39:10,369
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

489
00:39:10,409 --> 00:39:16,070
وَمَكَرُوا۟ مَكْرًا وَمَكَرْنَا مَكْرًا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ۝

490
00:39:16,110 --> 00:39:20,755
So they plotted a plot, and We planned a plan, while they perceived not.

491
00:39:21,275 --> 00:39:25,826
When these 9 men were meeting, they were meeting in secret, whispering to each other.

492
00:39:26,059 --> 00:39:28,193
But Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is listening to them.

493
00:39:29,507 --> 00:39:34,123
And they’re trying to hide their plan from Allah, but Allah is hearing their plan,

494
00:39:34,317 --> 00:39:38,920
but then Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is planning and His Plan is hidden from them.

495
00:39:39,511 --> 00:39:40,430
 مَكَرُوا۟ مَكْرًا

496
00:39:40,470 --> 00:39:45,447
They planned, but Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is also making a plan,

497
00:39:45,729 --> 00:39:50,405
but the Plan of Allah is secret and their plan is not because Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ is listening to them.

498
00:39:50,547 --> 00:39:59,207
فَٱنظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَـٰقِبَةُ مَكْرِهِمْ أَنَّا دَمَّرْنَـٰهُمْ وَقَوْمَهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ۝

499
00:39:59,247 --> 00:40:05,089
Then see how the end of their plot. Verily, we destroyed them and their nation altogether.

500
00:40:05,706 --> 00:40:06,536
Let’s go back.

501
00:40:06,986 --> 00:40:09,419
How many are the ones who made this plan?

502
00:40:10,063 --> 00:40:10,830
9.

503
