His father said;

683
00:53:22,674 --> 00:53:32,292
قَالَ أَرَاغِبٌ أَنتَ عَنْ ءَالِهَتِى يَـٰٓإِبْرَٰهِيمُ ۖ لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهِ لَأَرْجُمَنَّكَ ۖ وَٱهْجُرْنِى مَلِيًّا۝

684
00:53:32,371 --> 00:53:37,133
He, the father said: “Do you reject my gods, O Abraham?

685
00:53:37,335 --> 00:53:40,712
If you stop not, I will indeed stone you.

686
00:53:41,707 --> 00:53:45,310
So, get away from me safely before I punish you.

687
00:53:45,904 --> 00:53:47,795
He said: I will stone you, I’ll kill you.

688
00:53:48,660 --> 00:53:50,818
For a father to say this, it’s not easy.

689
00:53:52,051 --> 00:53:55,215
For a father to threaten his son that he’s gonna kill him is not easy,

690
00:53:56,131 --> 00:53:59,212
but this shows you the difference between kufr(كفر) and Eeman(إيمان).

691
00:53:59,645 --> 00:54:05,956
This shows you how bad relations could become when the separation is Eeman(إيمان) and kufr(كفر).

692
00:54:06,786 --> 00:54:08,762
The father is willing to kill the son.

693
00:54:09,840 --> 00:54:12,156
What was the response of Ibrahim(إبراهيم)? He said;

694
00:54:12,366 --> 00:54:18,776
قَالَ سَلَـٰمٌ عَلَيْكَ ۖ سَأَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّىٓ ۖ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ بِى حَفِيًّا ۝

695
00:54:18,816 --> 00:54:29,693
وَأَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَأَدْعُوا۟ رَبِّى عَسَىٰٓ أَلَّآ أَكُونَ بِدُعَآءِ رَبِّى شَقِيًّا۝

696
00:54:29,874 --> 00:54:34,565
Peace be upon you, I will ask Allah to forgive you.

697
00:54:34,933 --> 00:54:36,358
 إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ بِى حَفِيًّا

698
00:54:36,607 --> 00:54:39,313
He is, unto me, ever most Gracious.

699
00:54:40,099 --> 00:54:43,582
 Ibrahim(إبراهيم) is making istighfar(ٱستغفار) for someone who is a nonbeliever.

700
00:54:43,622 --> 00:54:44,986
Is that allowed in Islam?

701
00:54:45,866 --> 00:54:46,696
No.

702
00:54:47,886 --> 00:54:52,114
Obviously, at that time, Ibrahim عليه السلام did not know that.

703
00:54:53,232 --> 00:54:57,138
He promised his father that he will do Istighfar(ٱستغفار) for him, and he did Istighfar(ٱستغفار).

704
00:54:57,178 --> 00:54:58,236
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

705
00:54:58,276 --> 00:55:00,843
وَٱغْفِرْ لِأَبِىٓ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلضَّآلِّينَ۝

706
00:55:00,883 --> 00:55:04,859
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said: O Allah, forgive my father because he’s one of those misguided.

707
00:55:05,674 --> 00:55:10,478
But then Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ taught Ibrahim(إبراهيم) the truth, and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

708
00:55:10,518 --> 00:55:18,964
وَمَا كَانَ ٱسْتِغْفَارُ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ لِأَبِيهِ إِلَّا عَن مَّوْعِدَةٍ وَعَدَهَآ إِيَّاهُ

709
00:55:19,029 --> 00:55:25,187
فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُۥٓ أَنَّهُۥ عَدُوٌّ لِّلَّهِ تَبَرَّأَ مِنْهُ ۚ

710
00:55:25,288 --> 00:55:29,967
إِنَّ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ لَأَوَّٰهٌ حَلِيمٌ۝

711
00:55:30,007 --> 00:55:31,288
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

712
00:55:31,551 --> 00:55:35,516
And Ibrahim’s invoking of Allah for his father’s forgiveness

713
00:55:35,869 --> 00:55:40,163
was only because of a promise he, Ibrahim, has made to his father.

714
00:55:41,022 --> 00:55:50,436
But when it became clear to him that he is an enemy of Allah, he disassociated himself from him.

715
00:55:50,956 --> 00:55:56,076
Verily, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was Awwah(أوَّاة) and was haleem(حليم).

716
00:55:56,249 --> 00:56:02,260
Awwah(أَوَّاهٌ) is someone who always is in a state of khushoo(خشوع) and asking Allah سبحانه وتعالى and making Duʿa(دعاء) continuously,

717
00:56:02,484 --> 00:56:04,915
and Haleem(حَلِيمٌ) is someone who is forbearing.

718
00:56:05,680 --> 00:56:10,215
So Ibrahim(إبراهيم) only made Istighfar(ٱستغفار) for his father because of the promise,

719
00:56:10,287 --> 00:56:19,518
but when Ibrahim(إبراهيم) knew that his father is one of the nonbelievers and died on kufr (كفر), Ibrahim(إبراهيم) stopped.

720
00:56:20,947 --> 00:56:22,809
There is a hadith(حديث) mentioned in Bukhari(بخاري)

721
00:56:23,328 --> 00:56:29,094
that on the Day of Judgment, Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ will tell Ibrahim(إبراهيم) that

722
00:56:29,134 --> 00:56:36,522
I will fulfill My Promises on you and I will not dishonor you because Ibrahim(إبراهيم) has made a Duʿa(دعاء);

723
00:56:36,912 --> 00:56:38,499
وَلَا تُخْزِنِى يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُونَ

724
00:56:38,539 --> 00:56:40,847
O Allah, do not dishonor me on the Day of Resurrection.

725
00:56:40,887 --> 00:56:45,977
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ accepted the Duʿa(دعاء) of Ibrahim(إبراهيم), so He will not dishonor Ibrahim(إبراهيم) on the Day of Judgement.

726
00:56:46,677 --> 00:56:47,851
So Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said;

727
00:56:48,233 --> 00:56:53,168
What is a greater dishonor than punishing my father?

728
00:56:53,478 --> 00:56:57,482
Because the father of Ibrahim(إبراهيم) will come to him on the Day of Judgement

729
00:56:57,626 --> 00:56:58,872
and this is mentioned in Bukhari(بخاري)

730
00:56:59,113 --> 00:57:02,619
 the father of Ibrahim(إبراهيم) will come to Ibrahim(إبراهيم) on the Day of Judgement and tell him;

731
00:57:02,659 --> 00:57:06,032
Today, I will not disobey you, today, I will follow you.

732
00:57:07,372 --> 00:57:10,034
On the Day of Judgement, the father of Ibrahim(إبراهيم) will come and say;

733
00:57:10,171 --> 00:57:12,581
On this day, I will do whatever you want.

734
00:57:14,291 --> 00:57:18,354
At that moment, Ibrahim(إبراهيم) will tell Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎;

735
00:57:18,394 --> 00:57:21,572
How come my father could be punished?

736
00:57:22,758 --> 00:57:24,569
This is a dishonor to me.

737
00:57:26,178 --> 00:57:28,905
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ will tell Ibrahim(إبراهيم);

738
00:57:29,172 --> 00:57:30,495
Look at your father.

739
00:57:31,476 --> 00:57:40,518
So Ibrahim(إبراهيم) will look at his father and will find him in the form of Deeh(ضيح), Daba(الضبع) hyena.

740
00:57:41,456 --> 00:57:44,173
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) was talking with his father and then he made Duʿa(دعاء) to Allah.

741
00:57:44,213 --> 00:57:45,551
Allah told him: Look at your father,

742
00:57:45,591 --> 00:57:49,822
so Ibrahim(إبراهيم) will look at his father and find him in the form of a hyena.

743
00:57:50,493 --> 00:57:55,998
And then Ibrahim(إبراهيم) will walk away from him and the father will be thrown in Hellfire.

744
00:57:57,831 --> 00:58:09,283
Ibrahim(إبراهيم), when he was seeing his father in his physical form, it was difficult for him to have his father go to Hellfire.

745
00:58:10,646 --> 00:58:14,679
But, when the veils were lifted and Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ showed him the truth

746
00:58:15,446 --> 00:58:21,377
that this man is not your father, this man does not belong to you, this man is different,

747
00:58:21,702 --> 00:58:25,713
and his father even came in a different physical form,

748
00:58:25,873 --> 00:58:31,503
at that moment, Ibrahim(إبراهيم) walked away from his father and disassociated himself from him.

749
00:58:32,023 --> 00:58:33,860
And then Ibrahim(إبراهيم) told his father,

750
00:58:34,043 --> 00:58:37,001
after he told him: “I will ask Allah to forgive you,” he said;

751
00:58:37,145 --> 00:58:48,021
وَأَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَأَدْعُوا۟ رَبِّى عَسَىٰٓ أَلَّآ أَكُونَ بِدُعَآءِ رَبِّى شَقِيًّا۝

752
00:58:48,078 --> 00:58:54,915
And I shall turn away from you and from those whom you invoke besides Allah.

753
00:58:55,698 --> 00:58:57,199
وَأَعْتَزِلُكُمْ

754
00:58:57,682 --> 00:59:01,408
Aatizilukum(أَعْتَزِلُكُمْ) Means “I will disassociate myself from you,

755
00:59:01,706 --> 00:59:06,552
I will separate myself from you,I will be in seclusion from you,

756
00:59:07,331 --> 00:59:10,583
a very important principle for your survival as a Muslim.

757
00:59:10,878 --> 00:59:14,525
You have to have what is called ʿUzlah Shaʿuriyyah(عزلة الشعورية),

758
00:59:15,254 --> 00:59:20,873
psychological separation, from the environment of kufr(كفر) that is around you.

759
00:59:22,436 --> 00:59:27,517
Ibrahim عليه السلام immediately when his father chose kufr(كفر)

760
00:59:27,827 --> 00:59:33,162
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said that I will disassociate myself from you, the society of the nonbelievers.

761
00:59:33,819 --> 00:59:35,089
  وَأَعْتَزِلُكُمْ

762
00:59:35,276 --> 00:59:37,635
I will be separated from you.

763
00:59:39,028 --> 00:59:44,285
 We, as Muslims, have an identity that we have to protect

764
00:59:44,747 --> 00:59:50,035
and we cannot blend in with the society and be a sheep among the sheep,

765
00:59:50,618 --> 00:59:56,426
and follow the stream, and follow what everybody else is doing, and follow the crowd.

766
00:59:56,794 --> 01:00:01,238
We have an identity that we need to preserve and we need to be separate and different.

767
01:00:02,259 --> 01:00:06,264
But that doesn’t mean we have to separate ourselves physically from the society

768
01:00:06,304 --> 01:00:11,271
and live on monasteries on top of mountains or in the forests or in the deserts.

769
01:00:11,761 --> 01:00:12,324
No;

770
01:00:12,461 --> 01:00:18,467
we could be part of the society and be within the society, intermingling with the society,

771
01:00:18,633 --> 01:00:20,502
but in our hearts, we are separate.

772
01:00:21,548 --> 01:00:26,718
So, physically, we are actively participating in active participation with the society,

773
01:00:26,884 --> 01:00:31,230
but in our hearts we have this psychological barrier and separation

774
01:00:31,772 --> 01:00:36,865
where we always are carrying with us the understanding that we have an identity of being a Muslim.

775
01:00:37,702 --> 01:00:40,189
So, if you are able to be a part of this society

776
01:00:40,393 --> 01:00:45,367
but preserving your Muslim identity that is better than separating yourself physically from it

777
01:00:46,283 --> 01:00:52,918
because then you can be an agent of change and affecting others and Daʿwah(دعوة).

778
01:00:53,214 --> 01:00:58,164
But when you’re secluded and alone, you’re only benefiting yourself and nobody’s benefiting from the good that you have.

779
01:00:59,209 --> 01:01:01,330
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) made Daʿwah(دعوة) to his people also;

780
01:01:01,496 --> 01:01:12,076
إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوْمِهِۦ مَا هَـٰذِهِ ٱلتَّمَاثِيلُ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَنتُمْ لَهَا عَـٰكِفُونَ۝

781
01:01:12,184 --> 01:01:14,666
He said: What are these images to which you are devoted?

782
01:01:14,702 --> 01:01:16,123
What are these idols?

783
01:01:16,448 --> 01:01:18,475
And then he also told them in other Ayaat(آيات);

784
01:01:18,515 --> 01:01:22,083
قَالَ هَلْ يَسْمَعُونَكُمْ إِذْ تَدْعُونَ ۝ أَوْ يَنفَعُونَكُمْ أَوْ يَضُرُّونَ۝

785
01:01:22,767 --> 01:01:27,277
Do they hear you when you call on them or do they benefit you or harm you?

786
01:01:28,071 --> 01:01:29,909
Do they respond to your Duʿa(دعاء)?

787
01:01:29,974 --> 01:01:32,845
I mean, a god that does not respond to your Duʿa(دعاء), what god is he?

788
01:01:33,704 --> 01:01:35,486
And do they harm you or benefit you?”

789
01:01:35,717 --> 01:01:44,339
قَالُوا۟ بَلْ وَجَدْنَآ ءَابَآءَنَا كَذَٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُونَ۝

790
01:01:44,379 --> 01:01:47,086
They said: Nay, but we found our fathers doing so.

791
01:01:47,533 --> 01:01:50,754
They did not disapprove what Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said, they did not say;

792
01:01:51,184 --> 01:01:54,173
Yes, they do accept our duʿa, and yes, they do benefit us.

793
01:01:54,483 --> 01:01:57,181
No; they didn’t argue with that.

794
01:01:57,629 --> 01:02:01,512
Their response was; We’re doing this because our fathers were doing it.

795
01:02:02,226 --> 01:02:05,206
Just like when you talk to somebody: What’s your religion and why’re you doing this?

796
01:02:05,256 --> 01:02:11,514
He said: I was born a Christian, I was born Catholic. Don’t argue with me, I was born like that.

797
01:02:13,686 --> 01:02:19,068
This is Taqlid(تقليد) of Al-aba(الآباء), following the forefathers which Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ has mentioned in Qur'an;

798
01:02:19,108 --> 01:02:20,932
إِنَّهُمْ أَلْفَوْا۟ ءَابَآءَهُمْ ضَآلِّينَ ۝

799
01:02:21,120 --> 01:02:22,837
فَهُمْ عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَـٰرِهِمْ يُهْرَعُونَ۝

800
01:02:23,018 --> 01:02:27,063
They found their fathers misguided and they’re following their tracks.

801
01:02:29,270 --> 01:02:30,584
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said;

802
01:02:31,067 --> 01:02:40,206
قَالَ لَقَدْ كُنتُمْ أَنتُمْ وَءَابَآؤُكُمْ فِى ضَلَـٰلٍ مُّبِينٍ۝

803
01:02:40,264 --> 01:02:44,103
Indeed you and your fathers have been in manifest error.

804
01:02:45,055 --> 01:02:48,741
 Clear statements, he said that you are in error.

805
01:02:49,145 --> 01:02:52,767
This was a shock to the people; they couldn’t believe this statement, so they said;

806
01:02:53,070 --> 01:03:02,011
قَالُوٓا۟ أَجِئْتَنَا بِٱلْحَقِّ أَمْ أَنتَ مِنَ ٱللَّـٰعِبِينَ۝

807
01:03:02,307 --> 01:03:06,103
Are you bringing us the truth, or are you one of those who are playing around?

808
01:03:06,145 --> 01:03:07,420
They thought that he’s playing around.

809
01:03:07,460 --> 01:03:13,816
I mean, bluntly he’s saying that “you are wrong and your fathers are wrong, and these idols cannot do you any good and they’re false.”

810
01:03:14,509 --> 01:03:15,702
They said: “Are you joking?

811
01:03:16,214 --> 01:03:28,479
 قَالَ بَل رَّبُّكُمْ رَبُّ ٱلسَّمَـٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلَّذِى فَطَرَهُنَّ وَأَنَا۠ عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكُم مِّنَ ٱلشَّـٰهِدِينَ۝

812
01:03:28,519 --> 01:03:35,165
He said: Nay, your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth who created them, and of that I am one of the witnesses.

813
01:03:35,205 --> 01:03:35,852
 And he said;

814
01:03:35,932 --> 01:03:39,980
ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَنِى فَهُوَ يَهْدِينِ۝

815
01:03:40,225 --> 01:03:42,498
The One who created me so He will guide me.

816
01:03:42,671 --> 01:03:46,832
وَٱلَّذِى هُوَ يُطْعِمُنِى وَيَسْقِينِ۝

817
01:03:47,053 --> 01:03:49,480
And the One, Who feeds me and provides me with drink.

818
01:03:49,762 --> 01:03:53,344
وَإِذَا مَرِضْتُ فَهُوَ يَشْفِينِ۝

819
01:03:53,431 --> 01:03:56,201
And if I become ill, He is the One who cures me.

820
01:03:56,410 --> 01:04:00,972
وَٱلَّذِى يُمِيتُنِى ثُمَّ يُحْيِينِ۝

821
01:04:01,022 --> 01:04:04,507
The One who will make me die and the One who will give me life.

822
01:04:05,416 --> 01:04:08,163
This is the God that I worship, this is Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎.

823
01:04:09,910 --> 01:04:15,451
So Ibrahim(إبراهيم) told them that, I worship Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎, and Allah is your Lord and the Lord of the worlds,

824
01:04:15,624 --> 01:04:19,520
and then Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said silently to himself, he was speaking to himself;

825
01:04:19,917 --> 01:04:28,773
وَتَٱللَّهِ لَأَكِيدَنَّ أَصْنَـٰمَكُم بَعْدَ أَن تُوَلُّوا۟ مُدْبِرِينَ۝

826
01:04:28,860 --> 01:04:36,178
By Allah, I shall plot a plan to destroy your idols after you have gone away and turned your backs.

827
01:04:37,275 --> 01:04:38,192
He made a plan;

828
01:04:38,603 --> 01:04:40,782
he said: I am gonna destroy your gods.

829
01:04:42,139 --> 01:04:47,925
Somebody heard Ibrahim(إبراهيم) making that threat, but maybe they didn’t take it seriously.

830
01:04:48,993 --> 01:04:55,884
These people, they had a day in which they would go out of the town and they would celebrate.

831
01:04:55,924 --> 01:05:01,295
All of them would go out in their Jahiliyyah(جاهلية), ignorance, and they would go out in celebrations of Shayateen(شياطين).

832
01:05:01,728 --> 01:05:04,780
So they would go out of their town, all of them would go together.

833
01:05:05,422 --> 01:05:07,988
So they came to Ibrahim(إبراهيم) and told him: Come on, let’s go.

834
01:05:08,702 --> 01:05:09,705
فَقَالَ إِنِّى سَقِيمٌ۝

835
01:05:09,745 --> 01:05:11,393
He said: I am ill.

836
01:05:11,704 --> 01:05:13,393
He wasn’t physically ill.

837
01:05:16,092 --> 01:05:18,403
What he meant is that I am sick of what you’re doing.

838
01:05:19,853 --> 01:05:23,942
I am sick, he’s not physically sick, he said: I am sick of what you’re doing.

839
01:05:24,158 --> 01:05:28,253
They understood that he means that he is physically ill, so they allowed him to stay.

840
01:05:28,837 --> 01:05:33,484
But what he had in mind was that I’m sick of this worship that you are doing.

841
01:05:34,115 --> 01:05:38,402
So they left him alone thinking that he’s ill, and they all went out of town.

842
01:05:38,921 --> 01:05:42,834
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) followed through his plan; he took his axe

843
01:05:42,976 --> 01:05:49,255
and he went to the temple, he destroyed all of their idols except for the large, big one

844
01:05:49,360 --> 01:05:58,503
the humongous one, the biggest one, he left him intact, he destroyed all of the rest and then he hanged the axe on the shoulder of this large idol.

845
01:05:58,936 --> 01:06:00,686
He left this axe on his shoulder.

846
01:06:01,227 --> 01:06:04,171
They came back. Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

847
01:06:04,211 --> 01:06:10,409
فَجَعَلَهُمْ جُذَٰذًا إِلَّا كَبِيرًا لَّهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ إِلَيْهِ يَرْجِعُونَ۝

848
01:06:10,449 --> 01:06:15,464
So he broke them to pieces, all except the biggest of them that they might turn to it.

849
01:06:15,846 --> 01:06:17,852
So they came back; they looked at these idols, they said;

850
01:06:17,932 --> 01:06:28,602
قَالُوا۟ مَن فَعَلَ هَـٰذَا بِـَٔالِهَتِنَآ إِنَّهُۥ لَمِنَ ٱلظَّـٰلِمِينَ۝

851
01:06:28,667 --> 01:06:30,824
Who is the one who did this with our gods?

852
01:06:30,983 --> 01:06:33,227
 He must be indeed one of the wrongdoers.

853
01:06:33,465 --> 01:06:34,728
Who’s the one who did this?

854
01:06:35,204 --> 01:06:42,236
The one who heard Ibrahim(إبراهيم) speak, he came and said, actually it was more than one who heard Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

855
01:06:42,547 --> 01:06:51,958
  قَالُوا۟ سَمِعْنَا فَتًى يَذْكُرُهُمْ يُقَالُ لَهُۥٓ إِبْرَٰهِيمُ

856
01:06:52,232 --> 01:06:57,766
They said: We heard a young man talking against them who is called Ibrahim.

857
01:07:00,068 --> 01:07:02,246
Two things I want to turn your attention in this Ayah(آية);

858
01:07:03,386 --> 01:07:07,094
First of all, a young man, Fata(فتى), young man.

859
01:07:08,451 --> 01:07:09,309
He was young.

860
01:07:11,153 --> 01:07:18,210
This is the responsibility that the youth need to realize that major changes and Daʿwah(دعوة) that was done, were done by the young.

861
01:07:19,502 --> 01:07:20,721
The second thing;

862
01:07:22,041 --> 01:07:27,436
When, for example, I’m speaking with you and I’m telling you: Muhammad(محمد) called you,

863
01:07:29,016 --> 01:07:33,667
it’s different than if I say: A guy named Muhammad(محمد) called you.

864
01:07:33,940 --> 01:07:35,491
What’s the difference between the two?

865
01:07:36,509 --> 01:07:41,289
If I tell you: Muhammad(محمد) called you, or I tell you: A guy named Muhammad(محمد), he called you?

866
01:07:42,176 --> 01:07:46,656
If I tell you: Muhammad(محمد) called you, both of us know who Muhammad(محمد) is.

867
01:07:47,068 --> 01:07:49,767
When I tell you that a guy named Muhammad(محمد) called you,

868
01:07:49,977 --> 01:07:53,353
it’s either both of us or one of us doesn’t know who Muhammad(محمد) is.

869
01:07:54,876 --> 01:07:59,341
Over here, they said: We heard a young man called Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

870
01:07:59,370 --> 01:08:02,480
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) wasn’t even known to the society.

871
01:08:02,877 --> 01:08:07,062
He was a young boy; he wasn’t even known to the society

872
01:08:07,102 --> 01:08:12,613
and he’s coming up with this change that will bring down a whole society,

873
01:08:13,205 --> 01:08:15,932
carrying all of this load on his shoulders.

874
01:08:16,639 --> 01:08:23,272
A young boy, carrying all of this load on his shoulder, going against the whole society.

875
01:08:24,505 --> 01:08:32,905
قَالُوا۟ فَأْتُوا۟ بِهِۦ عَلَىٰٓ أَعْيُنِ ٱلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْهَدُونَ۝

876
01:08:32,945 --> 01:08:37,821
They said: Then bring them before the eyes of the people that they may testify.

877
01:08:38,153 --> 01:08:48,372
They gathered all of the people, and they wanted to bring Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and put him in court in front of everyone.

878
01:08:49,165 --> 01:08:51,081
So they brought everyone, and they said;

879
01:08:51,247 --> 01:09:01,237
قَالُوٓا۟ ءَأَنتَ فَعَلْتَ هَـٰذَا بِـَٔالِهَتِنَا يَـٰٓإِبْرَٰهِيمُ۝

880
01:09:01,286 --> 01:09:03,712
Are you the one who did this against our gods?

881
01:09:04,123 --> 01:09:05,083
He said: No.

882
01:09:05,710 --> 01:09:11,527
قَالَ بَلْ فَعَلَهُۥ كَبِيرُهُمْ هَـٰذَا فَسْـَٔلُوهُمْ

883
01:09:11,895 --> 01:09:17,175
 فَسْـَٔلُوهُمْ إِن كَانُوا۟ يَنطِقُونَ۝

884
01:09:17,225 --> 01:09:20,790
No, it’s not me. It’s the big idol who did it, so go and ask him.

885
01:09:22,385 --> 01:09:26,508
That was the point of the lesson, that’s the point that Ibrahim(إبراهيم) wants to drive home.

886
01:09:27,648 --> 01:09:31,234
Go and inquire from your gods.

887
01:09:31,378 --> 01:09:32,952
Let them tell you what happened.

888
01:09:33,587 --> 01:09:37,144
If you believe that your gods can do anything, then maybe the big one did it.

889
01:09:37,411 --> 01:09:40,723
If you believe that your gods cannot do anything, then why are you worshipping them?

890
01:09:42,000 --> 01:09:45,100
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said: Nay, this one, the biggest of them did it.

891
01:09:45,168 --> 01:09:46,758
Ask them, if they can speak.

892
01:09:47,036 --> 01:09:49,566
Ask them, if they can speak, this is the whole point.

893
01:09:50,281 --> 01:09:51,644
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

894
01:09:52,142 --> 01:10:01,996
فَرَجَعُوٓا۟ إِلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمْ فَقَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّكُمْ أَنتُمُ ٱلظَّـٰلِمُونَ۝

895
01:10:02,026 --> 01:10:03,801
So they turned to themselves, and said;

896
01:10:03,891 --> 01:10:07,170
Verily, you are the wrongdoers.

897
01:10:07,798 --> 01:10:09,060
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) woke them up.

898
01:10:09,255 --> 01:10:17,742
This was a shock to them, so for a moment, they woke up and realized their insanity and their mistake and their foolishness.

899
01:10:18,031 --> 01:10:20,169
So, they started to think about their position,

900
01:10:20,566 --> 01:10:24,507
but then Shaytan(شيطان) came in with his influence and his waswasah(وسوسة),

901
01:10:25,027 --> 01:10:29,920
so he made them override that thought, and they went back to their ignorance again.

902
01:10:29,950 --> 01:10:34,248
They woke up for a while, but then they lost the opportunity, and they said;

903
01:10:34,387 --> 01:10:35,232
Allah سبحانه وتعالى‎ says;

904
01:10:35,292 --> 01:10:36,595
ثُمَّ نُكِسُوا۟ عَلَىٰ رُءُوسِهِمْ

905
01:10:36,775 --> 01:10:38,740
Then they turned on their heads,

906
01:10:38,800 --> 01:10:45,051
meaning, they were going on the right way, they were starting to think, but then they fell down on their heads upside down.

907
01:10:45,231 --> 01:10:48,521
ثُمَّ نُكِسُوا۟ عَلَىٰ رُءُوسِهِمْ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَا هَـٰٓؤُلَآءِ يَنطِقُونَ۝

908
01:10:48,687 --> 01:10:50,881
And they said: You know that they cannot speak.

909
01:10:51,278 --> 01:10:53,757
They said: You know that they cannot speak.

910
01:10:54,039 --> 01:10:55,063
Ibrahim(إبراهيم) said;

911
01:10:55,294 --> 01:11:04,340
قَالَ أَفَتَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَنفَعُكُمْ شَيْـًٔا وَلَا يَضُرُّكُمْ ۝

912
01:11:04,774 --> 01:11:13,315
أُفٍّ لَّكُمْ وَلِمَا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ ۖ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ۝

913
01:11:13,345 --> 01:11:19,117
Do you then worship besides Allah things that can neither profit you nor harm you?

914
01:11:19,348 --> 01:11:23,261
Fie upon you, and upon that which you worship besides Allah.

915
01:11:23,398 --> 01:11:25,432
Have you then no sense?

916
01:11:26,226 --> 01:11:28,210
You have no understanding, no thinking.

917
01:11:28,470 --> 01:11:33,890
You’re worshipping gods that cannot speak, cannot do you any harm, cannot even defend themselves

918
01:11:34,049 --> 01:11:36,827
how can they defend you when they’re not able to defend themselves?

919
01:11:36,971 --> 01:11:41,632
These gods are lying dead on the ground, they can’t even help themselves.

920
01:11:44,504 --> 01:11:46,980
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّم

